<header class="sp-head"><p class="featured-region">4 March 1865 · Washington, D.C.</p><h1 class="sp-title">Lincoln's Second Inaugural Address</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>With the Union close to victory, Lincoln began his second term not in triumph but with a reflection on the shared guilt of North and South for slavery, and a call for reconciliation.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>Key passage</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>With malice toward none, with charity for all...</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">Second Inaugural Address, 4 March 1865.</p><div class="sp-full"><a class="sp-full-link" href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Abraham_Lincoln%27s_Second_Inaugural_Address" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the complete text<span aria-hidden="true"> &#8599;</span></a><span class="sp-full-src">Wikisource</span></div></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>Six weeks later Lincoln was assassinated, and the generous reconciliation he had urged gave way to a bitter struggle over Reconstruction and the rights of the freed people.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assassination-of-abraham-lincoln">Assassination of Abraham Lincoln</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconstruction-era">Reconstruction era</a></div></div></section>
